sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In early periods of earth's history, when forms of life were fewer and simpler, the rate of organic change was probably slower, and at the first dawn of life it may have been extremely slow.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rate of organic change was slower early in life's history";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XIV, “Recapitulation and Conclusion”; section “Effects of its adoption on the study of Natural history”. Scope: life on earth across its whole history"
}
